    "q-88548": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88548",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two independent events such that $P(A)=0.85$ and $P(B)=0.2.$ Find $P(A\\cap B).$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $A$ and $B$ are independent events, we can use the multiplication law for independent events, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cap B) & =P(A)\\cdot P(B) \\\\  & =0.85\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.17\\end{aligned}\n$$",
